<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank buys Hungary's Eurocorp.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank buys Hungary's Eurocorp.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Commerzbank AG said on Friday it had bought 51 percent of Hungary's Eurocorp International on October 1 and renamed the company EurocorpCommerz.</p>
<p>Budapest-based Eurocorp is a corporate finance company with special experience in the Hungarian capital market, Commerzbank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The purchase, which follows Commerzbank's takeover of Poland's Bank Rozvoju Eksportu and Wood &amp; Company of the Czech Republic, marks another strengthening of the German bank's investment banking activities in Central Europe, the statement said.</p>
<p>Commerzbank did not reveal the purchase price.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
